// MARIE program - Sensor Reading 12 bits/ms
// Store 50 elements

Load Addr // We load the address of the first element
Store Next // Create a pointer

Loop, Input
Store Value // User enters input and MARIE stores it

Load Value
StoreI Next // Store the AC value in the address of Next

// Go to the next position in memory
Load Next 
Add One
Store Next 

Load Count // Count = 0, declared below
Add One // Add one for each element to know how many we have
Store Count

Subt Elements // Substract 50 from count (AC)
SkipCond 400// If 0, it finishes
Jump Loop // If not 0, it continues

Halt

Addr, HEX 200 // So it does not collapse between instructions and inputs
Next, HEX 0
Value, DEC 0
Count, DEC 0
Elements, DEC 50 // Already declared 
One, DEC 1

